<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56877" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρκουρ-ος</span></b>  (proparox.) or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κερκοῦρος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>light vessel, boat</i>, esp. of
			the Cyprians, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.97
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Din.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				12.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Moschio
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				5.208e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				24.1
			</span></i> (pl.); used for Nile transport, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				54.3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, etc.:—written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρκυρος</span></b>  (as if from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κέρκυρα</span>) Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				142
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέρκυρα</span></b>  (pl.) <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ναξιουργὴς κάνθαρος</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a
			<i>sea-fish</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.141
			</span></i>. (Cf. Lat. <i>cercurus, cercyrus</i> in both
		senses.)</div>
